--- body ---
## Context

Five branches carry unmerged commits from 2026-08-14, each with a worktree
still registered. They are abandoned starts, not merged work: nothing on main
contains them, and each branch is the only copy of its commits. Four of them
name tickets that are still open and still listed as ready, so the next
session to pick one of those tickets will redo work that already exists.

The state file has flagged this since 2026-08-26 as a note to check the
branches. This ticket is that check, made actionable, because the risk grew:
main advanced by roughly 300 files in the three weeks since, and one of the
five now overlaps a change merged on 2026-09-06.

Measured 2026-09-06, after the catch-up that merged nine merge requests:

| branch | commits | ticket | size | merges into main today |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `t0359-hermetic-bash-test-children` | 1 | 0359, open | 212 lines, 5 test files | clean |
| `t0425-typo-fine-finition` | 1 | 0425, open | 275 lines, 12 files, adds `rules/typo/` | 1 conflict hunk |
| `t0500-leading-dash-project-name` | 2 | 0500, open | 560 lines, 7 files | clean |
| `t393-openrouter-seat-credential` | 4 | 0393, open | 439 lines, 6 files | clean |
| `memory-rtk-mechanism-correction` | 3 | none | 81 lines, 3 memory files | 3 conflict hunks |

## The two findings that make this more than a branch list

**Main already carries part of 0393, and the branch predates today's fix to
the same file.** `skills/reviewers/reviewers.sh` was 614 lines at the common
base, is 796 on the branch, and is 636 on main. Main has `--credential-env`
(8 occurrences) but none of the branch's keystore resolution (12
occurrences). Main also has the `attempted` counter from ticket 0870, merged
2026-09-06, which the branch does not have. So the branch is partly redundant
and partly ahead, against a file that has moved underneath it.

A three-way merge reports this branch as **clean**, and that is exactly the
trap `rules/git.md` names under the multi-PR wave: large edits in disjoint
regions auto-merge with no conflict and silently drop nothing here, but a
careless conflict resolution or a rebase that takes the branch's whole file
would revert 0870. Whoever picks this up must grep the merged result for the
0870 markers (`attempted`, `no seat reviewed`, `This is not an approval`)
before committing, not trust the clean exit.

**The rtk memory branch has no ticket and conflicts.** Its three commits
correct the recorded mechanism of the rtk output defect, and one of its two
conflicting files (`feedback-worktree-perime-sert-une-version-ancienne.md`)
has since changed on main. The harness rule body in `rules/git.md` already
carries a long, hedged account of the same defect that states the cause is
not isolated. Reconcile the branch against that text rather than merging it
blind: the branch may be the correction the rule needs, or it may be
superseded by it.

## Relevant files

- the five branches above, on `origin`, each with a worktree under `.claude/worktrees/`
- `skills/reviewers/reviewers.sh` — the contended file, changed on main on 2026-09-06 by ticket 0870
- `rules/git.md` — holds the current account of the rtk defect the memory branch corrects
- `tickets/0359-*.erg`, `0425-*.erg`, `0500-*.erg`, `0393-*.erg` — the open tickets involved

## Actions

Per branch, in this order, cheapest first:

1. Read the branch's diff against its merge base and decide one of three
   outcomes: **revive** (rebase, finish, open a merge request), **harvest**
   (take the part that is still right, discard the rest), or **drop**
   (delete the branch, recording in the ticket why the approach was
   abandoned).
2. For a revive or harvest, verify against current main rather than against
   the branch's base. State explicitly what main already carries.
3. For `t393`, additionally grep the result for the three 0870 markers above
   and run `tests/test_reviewers.sh` before opening anything.
4. For the rtk memory branch, compare its text against the current
   `rules/git.md` account and decide whether it corrects or duplicates it.
5. Record the outcome in the named ticket's log, then delete the branch and
   prune its worktree.

## Test

- No new test. This is a triage of existing work; each revived branch carries
  its own tests, which must pass on the rebased result rather than on the
  three-week-old base.
- For `t393`, `tests/test_reviewers.sh` is the gate, and it must still show
  the three 0870 cases passing after any merge of that branch.

## Verification

- [x] Each of the five branches has a recorded outcome: revived, harvested, or dropped
- [x] Every dropped branch's reasoning is in its ticket's log before the branch is deleted
      — `memory-rtk-mechanism-correction` has no ticket, so its reasoning is in this
      ticket's log below, written before the deletion
- [x] `t393`'s result preserves the 0870 behaviour, proven by the test file and not by a clean merge exit
      — `tests/test_reviewers.sh` 72 passed / 0 failed on the merged result, containing all
      three 0870 cases; the three markers also grep present. Against today's main the
      three-way merge does NOT report clean, so the trap this ticket named did not fire the
      way it was predicted — the test is what settled it either way
- [ ] No worktree remains for a branch that was dropped
      — NOT done, and deliberately. The unattended run of 2026-09-07 was forbidden to remove
      or prune any worktree: other sessions were live under `.claude/worktrees/` and removing
      the wrong one orphans a running session. The five 14-August worktrees are still
      registered and are listed in this ticket's log as a manual step

## Invariants

- No branch is deleted before its work is either merged or explicitly judged
  not worth keeping. Each is currently the only copy of its commits.
- The 0870 fix on `skills/reviewers/reviewers.sh` survives any 0393 work.
- Tickets 0359, 0425, 0500 and 0393 stay open until their own exit criteria
  are met. This ticket closes when the triage is done, not when they are.

## Exit criteria

- [x] All five branches triaged and their outcomes recorded
- [x] The stale-branch bullet in `STATE.md` removed or rewritten to match reality
- [x] `make check` passes on anything revived — 1098 (0359), 1110 (0500), 1097 (0393)
